    "root_causes_grpo_below_sft_point_estimate": [
      "Prompt-pool saturation: 38/45 (84.4%) of Cohort-v1 GRPO prompts were already trained on in Stage-1 SFT (avg 7.87 verified trajectories/task across 3 epochs), driving online_ex_rate from 37.5% (step 2) to 81.25% by step 4 and leaving limited positive exploration headroom.",
      "Late-epoch KL drift on small pool: running 100 steps (~4.44 prompt passes at 2 prompts/step, logged as 2.22 dataset epochs) pushed Dense GRPO KL from 0.00037 (step 2) to 0.01510 (step 100) while mean online_ex_rate drifted from 49.72% (epoch <=1) to 45.98% (epoch >1).",
      "Gateway/conciseness vs multi-CTE anti-fanout trade-off: 4-stage dense reward lifted partition_pruning 1st-pass gateway compliance from 83.3% to 100.0% (0.0% invalid SQL) and solved SFT failures ja_11 and rd_10, while step/length penalties (mean 405.6 vs 440.2 tokens) cost 1 task each on verbose multi-CTE fanout_dedup (4/6 -> 3/6) and partition_pruning (4/6 -> 3/6).",
      "Dense vs Sparse reward necessity confirmed: Outcome-Only Sparse GRPO suffered group-wise zero-variance advantage starvation on 32.0% of logged steps (16/50 vs 3/50 in Dense, 5.33x higher) and collapsed to 0.0% (0/6) on retention_date_math."
    ],
    "actionable_next_stage_protocol": [
      "Expand GRPO prompt pool from 45 (Cohort-v1) to 72+ (Cohort-v2 v1 + Hard-v2 + external schemas) and reserve non-upsampled prompts for RL.",
      "Apply dynamic pass@G curriculum filtering (retain prompts with 0 < pass@8 < 1 under pi_SFT) to eliminate saturated/zero-variance rollouts.",
      "Apply early checkpoint selection around 0.8-1.0 epoch before KL > 0.008 and relax length_free_chars (1400 -> 2400) for multi-CTE anti-fanout SQL."
    ]
